        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3358da78-1875-5969-9da5-033f5a7f4760",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Messiah Part II, Messiah (HWV 56)\n- People: George Frideric Handel, Jesus, Mary, Herod the Great\n- Concepts: Nativity of Jesus, birth of Jesus\n- Texts: Gospels of Luke and Matthew\n- Places: Bethlehem\n\nFacts:\n- In 1741, George Frideric Handel composed the English-language oratorio Messiah (HWV 56).\n- Messiah (HWV 56) is structured in three parts.\n- The listing for Messiah Part II presents Part II in a table and comments on individual movements, reflecting the relation of the musical setting to the text.\n- Part I of Messiah begins with the prophecy of the Messiah and his birth, includes the annunciation to the shepherds, and reflects the Messiah's deeds on earth.\n- The Nativity of Jesus, or birth of Jesus, is described in the Gospels of Luke and Matthew.\n- The accounts in Luke and Matthew agree that Jesus was born in Bethlehem during the time of Herod the Great to Mary, a betrothed virgin.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7a9e1a03-49bb-53f5-8c56-febf1431d612",
        "text": "Page: Messiah Part II. Sentence: Messiah (HWV 56), the English-language oratorio composed by George Frideric Handel in 1741, is structured in three parts.\nPage: Messiah Part II. Sentence: This listing covers Part II in a table and comments on individual movements, reflecting the relation of the musical setting to the text.\nPage: Messiah Part II. Sentence: Part I begins with the prophecy of the Messiah and his birth, shows the annunciation to the shepherds and reflects the Messiah's deeds on earth.\nPage: Nativity of Jesus. Sentence: The nativity of Jesus or birth of Jesus is described in the gospels of Luke and Matthew.\nPage: Nativity of Jesus. Sentence: The two accounts agree that Jesus was born in Bethlehem in the time of Herod the Great to a betrothed virgin whose name was Mary.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
